  {
    "id": "bhagavad-gita_17_4",
    "text_slug": "bhagavad-gita",
    "chapter": 17,
    "verse": 4,
    "original": "यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः |\nप्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः ||१७-४||",
    "transliteration": "yajante sāttvikā devānyakṣarakṣāṃsi rājasāḥ .\npretānbhūtagaṇāṃścānye yajante tāmasā janāḥ ||17-4||",
    "meaning": "17.4 The Sattvic or the pure men worship the gods; the Rajasic or the passionate worship the Yakshas and the Rakshasas; the others (the Tamasic or the deluded people) worship the ghosts and the hosts of the nature-spirits.",
